    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Cramer&#x27;s rule gives every unknown as a ratio of two determinants, x_i = det(A_i) / det(A). It is exact in theory but needs n + 1 determinants, each an O(n^3) factorization, so its cost grows like n^4 against elimination&#x27;s n^3.">

